libstdoc
-----------

libstdoc is a library for the C programming language.

libstdoc aims to be fast, customizable and safe, while maintaining
performance and control close to the traditional GNU C library
(glibc).

It is freestanding: it supplies its own entry point, its own formatted
output and its own allocator, and links without a C runtime.  The target
is Linux on aarch64; any other operating system or architecture is
rejected when the project is configured, rather than silently mapped
onto an implementation that does not match it.

Project Status
-----------------

libstdoc is currently in the beta stage: the current release is
1.0.0-beta (see NEWS).

The library is under active development and is not yet considered stable.
standard library, library internals, and project structure may change
frequently until the final 1.0.0 release.

Repository Structure
-----------------------
assembly/     Source Code of Assembly
io/           Source Code of Input Output
mem/          Source Code of Memory
etc/          Project configuration files
include/      Global include file
docs/         Documentation
test/         Test with pure C
build/        manual build directory

Documentation
----------------------

The docs/ directory documents the whole repository in plain text, in
the style of this file.  Start with docs/README, which lists every
document and the reading order for a first-time reader.

